{
  "configuration_id": "config_030",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best result so far is config_005 (RNA-only, multi-profile, scvi_n200, avgpool) at 0.650 acc / 0.628 F1, showing that scvi_n200 with avgpool aggregation is the strongest RNA configuration. Separately, config_018 (multimodal, multi-profile, PCA, ResNet50, avgpool, concat) at 0.619 shows a modest boost over its RNA-only counterpart config_002 (0.591), suggesting image adds ~3 pts with a weaker RNA encoder. Uncertainty: We do not know whether adding ResNet50 image still helps when the RNA side is already strong (scvi_n200), or whether the weak image signal (image-only acc only 0.208) becomes irrelevant or even detrimental. Question tested: Does the multimodal fusion of scvi_n200 (best RNA) + ResNet50 (best tested image) with avgpool and concat outperform the RNA-only scvi_n200 baseline? This is a single-variable extension of config_005 (adding the image modality), isolating the marginal contribution of image given an optimal RNA pipeline. Why best use of budget: The answer directly determines whether to invest remaining experiments in multimodal variants (configs 031-051) or to focus on RNA-only encoder/aggregation refinements. It is the highest-information experiment because it resolves the central design question—does multimodality add value on top of the best unimodal model—before committing to a large family of multimodal configurations."
}

